## Source and scope boundaries

The requested GICS09 Communication Services scope controls this edition. Industrials and GICS10 wording in the reused brief is a template carryover. Enterprise research and existing Notion child cases are supporting sources, distinct from the Origin Story editions added above.

HR02a Recruiting and HR02b Onboarding remain separate source pages, connected to one 120-minute HR02 sprint. HR09 source 1 is [People Analytics](https://app.notion.com/p/3d0ce6de608981a5ba59fc50d6dc7ba6). **HR09 source 2: not located after discovery; no link invented.** The [workforce blueprint](https://github.com/nbnayak88/successlabs-case-studies/blob/main/09-communication-services/omniconnect-media-networks-ltd/derived-streams/01-workforce.md) is supporting enterprise material, not a substitute for the missing second case.

[Enterprise hub](https://app.notion.com/p/00cc6a07fc6d409192495674373006e6) · [GICS02 reference](https://github.com/nbnayak88/learning-township/blob/main/01-HR-Human-Capital-Capability-Academy-Workforce-Monday/materials-origin-stories.md)

Historical windows are closed teaching groupings: 1970–1984, 1985–1994, 1995–2004, 2005–2014 and 2015–2025. Adoption overlaps and older practices can coexist today. AI exploration uses separate scenarios: 2026–2030 Assist, 2031–2040 Connect and 2041–2050 Adapt. These are not predictions or product roadmaps.

Pre-Foundation through Ultimate are learning handoffs in this publication, not completed deeper editions. Ultimate should conclude the story with value realization, cost/ROI assumptions, challenges, troubleshooting and lessons learned.

Saved-content readback does not establish automatic synchronization, public student access, successful copying, executed tabletop tests or operational outcomes. Observed-result fields remain empty. Existing OCN-P and OCN-M identifiers are preserved; OCN-XL identifiers are new educational additions. Existing source gaps and targets remain unresolved or unvalidated as labelled in the source register.

