## Beginner vocabulary

| Term | Meaning in these stories |
|---|---|
| NOC | Network Operations Centre, which monitors and coordinates service operations. |
| IAM | Identity and access management, which administers accounts and entitlements under approved policy. |
| OSS | Operations support systems, which manage network and service operations evidence. |
| Effective date | When an approved business change becomes valid, distinct from when it was entered or transmitted. |
| Tabletop test | A paper or discussion exercise that records a proposed response to synthetic evidence. |

The twelve HR themes organize learning subjects. The twelve architecture streams organize architectural viewpoints. Enterprise transformation streams organize cross-functional transformation work. These classification axes remain separate.
